WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:02.160
Instructor: Now, one last important note about tags

00:02.160 --> 00:03.810
has to do with pushing.

00:03.810 --> 00:06.725
By default, when you push up changes to a remote repository,

00:06.725 --> 00:09.065
tags are not going to be included.

00:09.065 --> 00:12.480
So you can push tags, actually, two different ways.

00:12.480 --> 00:14.610
You can push all of your tags that are new,

00:14.610 --> 00:18.109
using --tags, or you can go to Git Docs,

00:18.109 --> 00:22.248
and they talk about how you can push a single particular tag

00:22.248 --> 00:25.050
like this, git push, and then a remote name,

00:25.050 --> 00:27.300
and then the tag you want to push up.

00:27.300 --> 00:29.550
So I'll demonstrate this, but the problem is,

00:29.550 --> 00:32.400
right now, I just cloned the React repo.

00:32.400 --> 00:35.670
I can't push anything, tags or anything at all,

00:35.670 --> 00:36.720
because I don't have permission.

00:36.720 --> 00:37.950
I'm not a collaborator.

00:37.950 --> 00:39.661
So I'm gonna make my own repo.

00:39.661 --> 00:43.285
I'll just call this one tags-demo.

00:43.285 --> 00:45.360
Sure, I'll make it public.

00:45.360 --> 00:46.193
It doesn't matter.

00:46.193 --> 00:49.530
All I'm going to do is push up all of this here.

00:49.530 --> 00:53.010
I'm gonna push up React, but I'm gonna push it to my repo.

00:53.010 --> 00:55.267
So I'm gonna add a new remote.

00:55.267 --> 00:58.988
So I already have remote called origin because I cloned.

00:58.988 --> 01:00.944
So instead of renaming origin,

01:00.944 --> 01:05.944
I'll just go with git remote add, how about Colt?

01:05.947 --> 01:08.910
That is the name of my remote now.

01:08.910 --> 01:10.140
So I have two.

01:10.140 --> 01:11.370
This is Facebook's.

01:11.370 --> 01:14.040
Because I cloned, it just came with that remote.

01:14.040 --> 01:16.050
And then this is the one I just added.

01:16.050 --> 01:21.050
So now if I try and push up to mine, git push colt master,

01:22.136 --> 01:24.363
it's gonna take a while.

01:25.650 --> 01:27.571
But eventually, when that finishes,

01:27.571 --> 01:30.300
I'll refresh here, and...

01:30.300 --> 01:32.730
It's gonna be like a minute or so.

01:32.730 --> 01:33.840
I'll edit this out.

01:33.840 --> 01:35.220
It's still going.

01:35.220 --> 01:37.590
Oh, oh, something new.

01:37.590 --> 01:39.849
And that should be it, right?

01:39.849 --> 01:42.120
Okay. Whew.

01:42.120 --> 01:43.842
I'll refresh on GitHub.

01:43.842 --> 01:45.540
Great.

01:45.540 --> 01:47.407
Hmm. I don't see any tags.

01:47.407 --> 01:50.190
Hopefully, you see that right there. Zero tags.

01:50.190 --> 01:53.370
So all the work, everything that I cloned from git,

01:53.370 --> 01:55.650
or sorry, everything I cloned from React,

01:55.650 --> 01:57.891
is pushed up but not tags.

01:57.891 --> 02:01.020
So I can push one tag up at a time.

02:01.020 --> 02:04.080
If we just pick one, like, oh, mytag,

02:04.080 --> 02:05.130
that was one we created,

02:05.130 --> 02:08.346
I can do git push origin, and then a tag name.

02:08.346 --> 02:10.410
Well, I can't push the origin.

02:10.410 --> 02:11.310
What a mess.

02:11.310 --> 02:15.230
I can push to my remote rather that I created called colt.

02:15.230 --> 02:17.940
And that should be quick.

02:17.940 --> 02:20.560
Hopefully, we're just pushing up a single tag.

02:20.560 --> 02:23.688
And there it is, mytag.

02:23.688 --> 02:26.469
But if I wanna push up all tags,

02:26.469 --> 02:30.074
that's where we can use the --tags flag.

02:30.074 --> 02:33.630
So I still need to specify, in this case, where.

02:33.630 --> 02:36.300
So I didn't use the -u option when I pushed,

02:36.300 --> 02:38.250
so I haven't set an upstream for this branch,

02:38.250 --> 02:42.660
but I'll do git push colt and then --tags.

02:42.660 --> 02:44.610
So colt is my remote name,

02:44.610 --> 02:47.128
obviously not a very conventional name.

02:47.128 --> 02:50.100
But because I didn't fork and then clone this,

02:50.100 --> 02:51.480
I had to add a remote.

02:51.480 --> 02:54.150
I could have changed the origin remote

02:54.150 --> 02:55.770
to point to my repo instead.

02:55.770 --> 02:57.210
But anyway, it doesn't matter.

02:57.210 --> 03:01.583
If I do --tags, it now pushes up to my repository,

03:01.583 --> 03:05.460
that remote, and it's going to push all of those tags up.

03:05.460 --> 03:08.100
Should be nowhere near as as much time, though.

03:08.100 --> 03:11.790
This is maybe 10 seconds or so compared to a minute,

03:11.790 --> 03:13.050
which is what we had earlier.

03:13.050 --> 03:16.440
And there we go, 141 tags. They're pushed up.

03:16.440 --> 03:17.610
So moral of the story.

03:17.610 --> 03:20.010
Tags are not included by default when you push.

03:20.010 --> 03:21.660
You can push them one at a time,

03:21.660 --> 03:25.260
or you can push all tags in a repo using --tags.

03:25.260 --> 03:27.150
And that about wraps it up for tags.

03:27.150 --> 03:30.004
A pretty simple feature, but also very heavily used,

03:30.004 --> 03:33.327
and especially in large projects, open-source projects

03:33.327 --> 03:36.630
and tightly tied, at least in how they're commonly used,

03:36.630 --> 03:39.330
tightly tied to semantic versioning.

03:39.330 --> 03:40.323
So that's tags.
